      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:78:15",
      "text": [
        " مَا صَافَحَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) رَجُلًا قَطُّ فَنَزَعَ يَدَهُ حَتَّى يَكُونَ هُوَ الَّذِي يَنْزِعُ يَدَهُ مِنْهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from Ismail Bin Mihran, from Ayman Bin Muhriz, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>azwj</sup> did not shake the hand of a man at all and removed his<sup>saww</sup> hand away until he was the one who removed his hand from his<sup>saww</sup> (first)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "15. It is narrated from him (narrator of the Hadith above) from Isma’il ibn Mehran from Ayman ibn Muhriz from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “When shaking hands with people, the Messenger of Allah had never been the first to discontinue the handshake.” "
        ]
      }
